{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isDoor"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContainersDoorsAndLocks"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Either the map says so, by hanging a way through on the thing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hall.north(garden, via: frontDoor)"},{"type":"text","text":"), or the item declares "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/door","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The first covers every door a player can walk through, which is why most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"games never declare the second."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It answers the same for every room, which is deliberate. A rule that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"wants “a door ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"here"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"” — the one the player could walk through from where"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"they stand — wants the room’s exits, not this. What this is for is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"question a verb asks about the thing in front of it: knocking on a door"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is a different act from knocking on a bench, wherever either is standing."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isDoor"},"metadata":{"title":"isDoor","symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:6Gnusto4ItemV6isDoorSbvp","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isDoor"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"True if this item is a door — the front door, the trap door, the grating.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/isdoor"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/ContainersDoorsAndLocks":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContainersDoorsAndLocks","title":"Containers, Doors, and Locks","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/containersdoorsandlocks","abstract":[{"text":"Hold things, open and close, lock with keys, and gate the map.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/door":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"door"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9ItemTraitV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ItemTrait"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/door","title":"door","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/door","abstract":[{"text":"The item is a door — something a verb may reasonably treat as a way through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than as a thing.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item":{"abstract":[{"text":"A thing in the world.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item","title":"Item","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"title":"Gnusto","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto","abstract":[{"text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item/isDoor":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isDoor"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item\/isDoor","title":"isDoor","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item\/isdoor","abstract":[{"text":"True if this item is a door — the front door, the trap door, the grating.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"}}}